  "result": "I fixed `src/queue.js` so it follows the contract, and `npm test` passes with all 6 tests, including 4 new regression tests.\n\nThere were four bugs behind your three reports:\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never decremented `running`, so its slot was never freed and the queue stalled. A job that threw synchronously also broke the queue. Every outcome now frees the slot, and sync throws and plain return values are handled.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending, not that nothing was running. It now requires both.\n- **Only one job after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It is now a loop that fills every free slot, so `resume()` with concurrency 4 starts four.\n\nThe new tests in `test/queue.test.js` cover failures (async and sync), `onIdle()` with a job still running, resuming with concurrency 4, and pause behaviour.",
